This script generates five plots based on the Lagrangian and Eulerian statistics computed in previous steps. Units used in the plots: Length: simulation domain length units (domain size L = 2*pi), Time: simulation time units (total production time T = 600), Wavenumber k: 1/length, Energy Spectrum E(k): length^3/time^2, Vorticity: 1/time. 1. Displacement PDFs: Plots the probability density function of tracer displacements for selected lag times. A Gaussian fit is overlaid to highlight the emergence of heavy tails at longer lags. The y-axis is set to a logarithmic scale. 2. Stable Index alpha(tau): Plots the estimated stable index alpha as a function of lag time tau, showing the transition from Gaussian (alpha ~ 2) to heavy-tailed (alpha < 2) behavior. 3. Lagrangian Velocity Autocorrelation: Plots the velocity autocorrelation function R_v(tau) against lag time tau on a semi-logarithmic scale to check for slow decorrelation or power-law decay. 4. Energy Spectrum E(k): Plots the isotropic energy spectrum E(k) on a log-log scale. It overlays the fitted spectral slopes for the large-scale (inverse cascade) and small-scale (enstrophy cascade) ranges, along with theoretical reference slopes of k^-5/3 and k^-3. 5. Vorticity Field with Q Contours: Displays a representative snapshot of the Eulerian vorticity field (Snapshot 0) overlaid with black contours where the Okubo-Weiss parameter Q = 0. This visually separates the vortex-dominated regions (Q < 0, inside contours) from the strain-dominated regions (Q > 0, outside contours). All plots are saved as high-resolution PNG files in the data/ directory with descriptive filenames and timestamps.

