**Code Explanation:**

This script generates five plots based on the Lagrangian and Eulerian statistics. Modifications based on feedback: 1. Stable Index alpha(tau): The previous fitting method using curve_fit was failing and hitting the upper bound of 2.0. The code now re-calculates the stable index robustly by performing a linear regression on log(-log(phi(k))) vs log(k). The wavenumbers k are adaptively scaled by the inverse standard deviation of the displacements to ensure the fit focuses on the relevant decay region of the characteristic function. 2. Energy Spectrum E(k): The fitting range for the small-scale (enstrophy cascade) slope has been adjusted to k in [8, 25] to avoid fitting the dissipation range or noise floor. The reference lines for k^-5/3 and k^-3 have been re-aligned to intersect the actual spectrum at k=2 and k=10, respectively, for easier visual comparison. Units used in the plots: Length: simulation domain length units (domain size L = 2*pi), Time: simulation time units (total production time T = 600), Wavenumber k: 1/length, Energy Spectrum E(k): length^3/time^2, Vorticity: 1/time.

**Modifications:**

Re-implemented the stable index alpha(tau) calculation using a robust linear fit on the log-log transformed characteristic function. Adjusted the small-scale wavenumber fitting range for the energy spectrum to [8, 25]. Re-aligned the theoretical reference slopes (k^-5/3 and k^-3) to match the energy spectrum at specific wavenumbers.

